Here's the formal **testsmells.org 19-smell** audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, calibrated for integration-test scope.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means one branch never executes — you're silently skipping assertions depending on runtime type. This hides testing gaps.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests or assert deterministically:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← no assertions
```

**Problem:** This passes even if every insert silently fails (e.g., returns without persisting). False confidence.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Fixed 3-second sleep makes the suite slow and introduces flakiness (too short on slow CI, wasteful on fast machines). *Downgraded from High per integration-test calibration*, but still a smell — prefer polling.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent);
}
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, you must read the source to figure out *which* property was wrong.

**Fix — add messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should exist after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-generated");
```

---

## ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written)

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, clear assertion, minimal setup |
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Focused workflow, 2 clear assertions |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Self-documenting count (3 inserted → assert 3), uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Appropriate concurrency test with clear assertion |

The fixture itself (`[TestInitialize]`) is well-designed — in-memory SQLite avoids Mystery Guest, and both fields are used by all tests (no General Fixture smell).

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add count/content assertion | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into two deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace with poll/retry helper | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings | ~2 min |

**Bottom line:** 4 out of 8 tests are clean. The two High-severity smells (Conditional Test Logic, Assertion-Free) are the urgent ones — they can mask real bugs passing silently through CI.
